#
# Runs a command while holding the machine awake, for work `idle-poweroff`
# can't see on its own: work that outlives its ssh session, such as under
# `nohup` or `tmux`, or sends both its output and its errors elsewhere.
# `idle-poweroff` counts the lock `keep-awake` takes as work.
#
# Usage: `keep-awake COMMAND [ARGUMENTS...]`
exec systemd-inhibit --what=idle --who=keep-awake --why="$*" "$@"
